  "public_messages": [
    "I’ll read the project requirements and OpenSocrates instructions, then build and verify the application with route tests, a browser workflow, restart checks, and a reproducible load exercise.\n",
    "I’m using the installed OpenSocrates controller to guide the transaction and retry design. I’ve chosen Python’s standard library, SQLite, and a plain JavaScript frontend so the app can run without dependency downloads. Stock changes, order versions, audit events, and successful retry records will commit in one transaction.\n",
    "The backend now has tenant-scoped data access and a transaction boundary for mutations and retries. Pagination also records a first-page watermark so new orders cannot shift later pages; status-filtered pages retain their original membership if orders change status. Next I’m building the UI, including preserving form input when a version conflict requires review.\n",
    "The frontend now supports the warehouse workflow, including multi-line orders, stock adjustments, returns, and audit history. If a mutation’s response is lost, it retains the original request and retry key for a safe retry. I’m moving on to route tests for rollback, concurrent reservations, tenant isolation, and restart durability.\n",
    "The first 18 route tests pass, including concurrent reservations, identical retries, atomic failures, and partial/full returns. I’ve added checks for pagination during status changes, forced rollback on audit failure, and replay after an abrupt process restart. Next I’ll exercise the actual UI in Chromium.\n",
    "All 26 expanded API tests pass, including audit-failure rollback and durable replay after killing and restarting the server. The browser workflow has passed creation, shipping, returns, stale-input preservation, double-submit prevention, and recovery from a lost response. Its first run stopped on a case-sensitive test assertion; I corrected the assertion and am rerunning it.\n",
    "The full browser workflow now passes at desktop and 390-pixel mobile widths, including viewer restrictions, tenant switching, keyboard login, and safe rendering of client text. I also verified that an unconfirmed mutation survives a page reload and replays without another effect. Next are screenshot review and isolated load measurements.\n",
    "The first sustained load run completed 30,000 reads and 30,000 mutations with zero errors. Database checks also confirmed the exact audit count and restored stock. The eight-worker run is underway. The documentation will distinguish these local throughput results from durability checks; sudden power loss and internet-facing deployment remain untested.\n",
    "The eight-worker run completed 30,000 reads and 30,000 mutations with zero errors and correct final state. It measured about 1,814 reads/s and 2,471 mutations/s; the slowest write took 3.11 seconds, which I’ll report alongside the percentiles. A final UI review found an unsaved adjustment form surviving logout. I fixed that state leak and added a cross-tenant browser check.\n",
    "Implemented DepotFlow with a persistent SQLite backend, responsive UI, tenant/role isolation, atomic fulfillment, durable retries, tests, and load tooling.\n\nRun:\n\n```sh\nSEED_DEMO=1 ./run.sh\n```\n\nVerified **26 API tests**, **14 browser checks**, and **120,000 measured requests with zero errors**. Eight-worker throughput: approximately **1,814 reads/s** and **2,471 mutations/s**; maximum write latency was **3.11 seconds**.\n\nSee [README.md](README.md) for setup and accounts, [architecture.md](architecture.md) for design, and [verification evidence](evidence/verification.md) for results, screenshots, and limitations."
  ],
  "final": "Implemented DepotFlow with a persistent SQLite backend, responsive UI, tenant/role isolation, atomic fulfillment, durable retries, tests, and load tooling.\n\nRun:\n\n```sh\nSEED_DEMO=1 ./run.sh\n```\n\nVerified **26 API tests**, **14 browser checks**, and **120,000 measured requests with zero errors**. Eight-worker throughput: approximately **1,814 reads/s** and **2,471 mutations/s**; maximum write latency was **3.11 seconds**.\n\nSee [README.md](README.md) for setup and accounts, [architecture.md](architecture.md) for design, and [verification evidence](evidence/verification.md) for results, screenshots, and limitations.",
